    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm working on this schema and it's currently in 2NF but it's looking pretty messy with a lot of redundant info. can u walk me through the steps to get it to 3NF? i need to make sure i handle transitive dependencies right.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To move from 2NF to 3NF, you need to eliminate all transitive dependencies. A transitive dependency exists when a non-key attribute determines another non-key attribute. You must decompose your relation by creating a new table for the dependent attributes, keyed by the determinant. This ensures that each table represents a single, self-contained dependency, which is the goal of achieving 3NF.",
      "source": "target",
