      "content": "Yes, fundamentally, normalization is about structuring data to be more reliable and reduce redundancy, thereby preventing update anomalies. To check for 3NF readiness, first ensure the table is in 2NF (all non-key attributes depend on the *entire* primary key). Then, rigorously search for any non-key attribute that determines another non-key attribute; if you find any such transitive dependency, you need to decompose the table further.",
